# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: TyrantPath1

translate es strings:

    old "Do not listen to her!"
    new "¡No la escuches!"

    old "Seize Marion Achillea immediately!"
    new "¡Atrapa a Marion Achillea inmediatamente!"

    old "For a moment, there was confusion on the room, the soldiers unsure of whom to listen to."
    new "Por un momento, hubo confusión en la habitación, con los soldados indecisos sobre a quién obedecer."

    old "I am the king, and I order you to seize him!"
    new "Soy el rey y te ordeno que lo aprehendas!"

    old "This reminder was enough for the soldiers, and they moved again, grabbing Marion, wrestling him to the ground as he tried to fight them."
    new "Este recordatorio fue suficiente para los soldados, y volvieron a moverse, agarrando a Marion y lanzándolo al suelo mientras él intentaba luchar contra ellos."

    old "You promised! Is your word worth nothing!?"
    new "¡Lo prometiste! ¿Tu palabra no vale nada!"

    old "Marion's voice broke as he screamed. One of the soldiers cracked him across the mouth with his mailed fist."
    new "La voz de Marion se quebró mientras gritaba. Uno de los soldados le dio un puñetazo con su guante metálico en la boca."

    old "Blood and teeth splattered across the floor, and Marion slumped over. Either unconscious or too stunned to speak."
    new "Sangre y dientes salpicaron el suelo, y Marion se desplomó. ¿Inconsciente o demasiado aturdida para hablar?"

    old "The soldiers began to drag him away."
    new "Los soldados comenzaron a arrastrarlo hacia fuera."

    old "Thomas. I gave him my word he would be safe."
    new "Thomas. Le di mi palabra de que estaría a salvo."

    old "And you were smart to lie to him like that, but I won't allow him to escape for what he did."
    new "Y fuiste inteligente al mentirle de esa manera, pero no le permitiré que escape por lo que hizo."

    old "He tried to destroy our country, kill me, and if he had won, he would have killed you too."
    new "Intentó destruir nuestro país, matarme a mí, y si hubiera ganado, también te habría matado a ti."

    old "If we let him live in exile, it won't be long until he's back."
    new "Si lo dejamos vivir en el exilio, no pasará mucho tiempo hasta que regrese."

    old "Unlike father, I'm not going to let these problems fester. We rip the traitors out by the root, starting with Marion, the one who caused all of this."
    new "A diferencia de mi padre, no voy a permitir que estos problemas se pudran. Arrancaremos a los traidores por la raíz, empezando por Marion, quien causó todo esto."

    old "Sarah wanted to keep her word to Marion, but Thomas was right. He was the king, and his order stood over hers. There was nothing she could do."
    new "Sarah quería cumplir su palabra con Marion, pero Thomas tenía razón. Él era el rey y su orden prevalecía sobre la suya. No había nada que pudiera hacer."

    old "Still, it did not trouble Sarah that much."
    new "Sin embargo, eso no le causaba demasiada preocupación a Sarah."

    old "Her brother had been right. Marion would have killed her without thinking anything of it."
    new "Su hermano tenía razón. Marion la habría matado sin pensarlo dos veces."

    old "Whatever punishment was coming for him was entirely earned."
    new "Cualquier castigo que le fuera a llegar, estaba totalmente merecido."

    old "For now, this is where the game ends."
    new "Por ahora, aquí es donde termina el juego."
